#{[{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046644} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186518291} :activity/id #uuid "e3aa0f2d-b3b2-57fa-9b22-abb7f5a88662" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049282 :topic/id #uuid "e9af0219-7eb8-5b10-84c1-b7b5e8e30ae2" :topic/math-academy-id 3135} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186518291 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162356 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b7e37e95-9cea-5ab2-a140-cd13a369a582" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "252" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159339} {:answer/id #uuid "13a4b33f-6cc5-5cf7-ae67-11fc4cec69cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "272" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159340} {:answer/id #uuid "1a556378-662e-50f4-84e2-69704397f53e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "225" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159341} {:answer/id #uuid "26188799-c8bd-52c4-8204-93f83b48f701" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "127" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159342} {:answer/id #uuid "458d0deb-efd4-5187-a31c-bbfaa42d288f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "131" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159343}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186159343} :answer-field/id #uuid "35881875-1699-51c1-8367-015366562cfb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159338}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "fe1495c6-48c4-58ae-8df8-b0dc82576087" :question/math-academy-id "q-137888" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 \\\\ 8 & -6\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,W=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrices $A$ and $W,$ and the vector $b$ above. If the normal equation for the corresponding weighted least-squares problem $W\\,Ax=Wb$ is given by\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}a & -60 \\\\ -60 & b\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ c\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nwhat is the value of $a+b+c?$" :question/worked-solution "To get the normal equation corresponding to $W\\,Ax=Wb,$ we pre-multiply both sides of the equation by $(W\\,A)^{T}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(W\\,A)^{T}\\cdot W\\,Ax & =(W\\,A)^{T}\\cdot Wb \\\\ {A}^{T}({W}^{T}W)Ax & ={A}^{T}({W}^{T}W)b\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since\n\n$$\n{W}^{T}W=[\\begin{aligned}{1}^{2} & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & {2}^{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & {1}^{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nour normal equation can be written as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 0 & 8 \\\\ 3 & 0 & -6\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-4 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 \\\\ 8 & -6\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 0 & 8 \\\\ 3 & 0 & -6\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}-4 & 0 & 8 \\\\ 3 & 0 & -6\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-4 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 \\\\ 8 & -6\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 0 & 8 \\\\ 3 & 0 & -6\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 12 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}80 & -60 \\\\ -60 & 45\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=80+45+6=131.\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "bfe95e7b-6300-507c-9c3b-ebf83c2fe680" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186518292}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186518292 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186363141 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "31df6980-e28f-5655-96b0-97100c221864" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363143} {:answer/id #uuid "59cb2372-fcfd-5880-86f6-1039eff11d14" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363144} {:answer/id #uuid "c671ff9c-fe69-5b23-a1dd-adb41bd2e1eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363145} {:answer/id #uuid "4ccb097e-a30e-5c38-b41b-5b9e6dc56cd6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363146} {:answer/id #uuid "42cf4c5f-1c12-573f-baf0-000510385765" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363147}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186363146} :answer-field/id #uuid "862dc94f-3b95-5dca-bd86-c0c2d3c02b0f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363142}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "5018d743-6c3b-5485-b0a5-b9dd110b0784" :question/math-academy-id "q-137890" :question/problem "Find the solution for the weighted least-squares problem $W\\,Ax=Wb,$ where\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 27 \\\\ 27\\end{bmatrix},\\,W=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To get the normal equation corresponding to $W\\,Ax=Wb,$ we pre-multiply both sides of the equation by $(W\\,A)^{T}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(W\\,A)^{T}\\cdot W\\,Ax & =(W\\,A)^{T}\\cdot Wb \\\\ {A}^{T}({W}^{T}W)Ax & ={A}^{T}({W}^{T}W)b\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since\n\n$$\n{W}^{T}W=\\begin{bmatrix}{5}^{2} & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & {2}^{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & {2}^{2}\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}25 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nour normal equation can be written as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}25 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}25 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 27 \\\\ 27\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 25 \\\\ -4 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 108 \\\\ 108\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}8 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 29\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 108\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since the matrix on the left-hand side is invertible, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} & ={\\begin{bmatrix}8 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 29\\end{bmatrix}}^{-1}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 108\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8\\cdot 29-4\\cdot 4}\\begin{bmatrix}29 & -4 \\\\ -4 & 8\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 108\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{216}\\begin{bmatrix}-432 \\\\ 864\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "c33819f8-c46b-5dee-a664-df0a06fddca7" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186518300}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186518297 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186269157 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "50f20ae7-abd3-5f44-993f-508d38288225" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266868} {:answer/id #uuid "72c6ad65-aa21-5871-bbdd-ae9be001132a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267150} {:answer/id #uuid "7b668a07-a7f7-5301-a9ad-260bdef00bd7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267234} {:answer/id #uuid "b2a2dcef-70bc-513c-933f-5670bdbaeb08" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267743} {:answer/id #uuid "c5262c9a-0c15-5b79-95b3-1639a4ba997a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{8}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267910}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186267150} :answer-field/id #uuid "97862143-c8cb-59a2-ad09-aef226dfbf0a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268672}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "80a60424-3ff9-5896-996b-077192e08a91" :question/math-academy-id "q-137920" :question/problem "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 \\\\ -3 & -2\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}16 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix},\\,W=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nConsider the matrices $A$ and $W,$ and the vector $b$ shown above. If the general solution for the weighted least-squares problem $W\\,Ax=Wb$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}a \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}b \\\\ c\\end{bmatrix},\\,{x}_{2}\\in R,\n$$\n\nwhat is the value of  $a+\\frac{b}{c}?$" :question/worked-solution "To get the normal equation corresponding to $W\\,Ax=Wb,$ we pre-multiply both sides of the equation by $(W\\,A)^{T}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(W\\,A)^{T}\\cdot W\\,Ax & =(W\\,A)^{T}\\cdot Wb \\\\ {A}^{T}({W}^{T}W)Ax & ={A}^{T}({W}^{T}W)b\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since\n\n$$\n{W}^{T}W=\\begin{bmatrix}{1}^{2} & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & {2}^{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & {2}^{2}\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nour normal equation can be written as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 \\\\ -3 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}16 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 \\\\ -12 & -8\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}16 \\\\ -12 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}45 & 30 \\\\ 30 & 20\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}60 \\\\ 40\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the system corresponding to the above matrix equation using Gaussian elimination, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}45 & 30 & 60 \\\\ 30 & 20 & 40\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-\\frac{2}{3}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}45 & 30 & 60 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix above has one pivot column (the $1$st one). Thus, ${x}_{2}$ is a free variable. From the first equation, we have \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=\\frac{4}{3}-\\frac{2}{3}{x}_{2}.\n$$\n\nHence, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{4}{3}-\\frac{2}{3}{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{4}{3} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{2}{3} \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,{x}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+\\frac{b}{c}=\\frac{4}{3}+\\frac{(-\\frac{2}{3})}{1}=\\frac{2}{3}.\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "cfea7d4a-7abe-545a-885a-a12f28682791" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186518304}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186518300 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186269156 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "05570479-3181-5e57-96b6-4219c59cf564" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266191} {:answer/id #uuid "4e03678f-5f2c-50ab-ac7b-d8988b8729da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266836} {:answer/id #uuid "b2febfa5-ce27-5916-a5c7-126fd54f568b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267748} {:answer/id #uuid "bda4ad6d-280e-59db-aad9-e65da43be5b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267845} {:answer/id #uuid "c11f32dc-8223-5b6a-a3c7-6f9a6be65d94" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267869}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186266836} :answer-field/id #uuid "e3a390e1-866c-520b-b61b-4f91163c49d1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268807}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "670f8829-0bde-5ea3-bf13-816d75c51f2a" :question/math-academy-id "q-137917" :question/problem "Find the solution for the weighted least-squares problem $W\\,Ax=Wb,$ where\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix},\\,W=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To get the normal equation corresponding to $W\\,Ax=Wb,$ we pre-multiply both sides of the equation by $(W\\,A)^{T}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(W\\,A)^{T}\\cdot W\\,Ax & =(W\\,A)^{T}\\cdot Wb \\\\ {A}^{T}({W}^{T}W)Ax & ={A}^{T}({W}^{T}W)b\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since\n\n$$\n{W}^{T}W=\\begin{bmatrix}{2}^{2} & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & {1}^{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & {1}^{2}\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nour normal equation can be written as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-12 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}5 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-8 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since the matrix on the left-hand side is invertible, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} & ={\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}}^{-1}\\begin{bmatrix}-8 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5\\cdot 2-1\\cdot 1}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-8 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}\\begin{bmatrix}-18 \\\\ 18\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "d69dbc57-2846-5307-b0ec-b87f9e963a12" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186518297}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186518304 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186518129 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "345c0919-c48a-51ec-93ba-67d74c6a767d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "42" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517587} {:answer/id #uuid "79e70a70-5d0e-5891-8648-6f2603f7c863" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "34" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517718} {:answer/id #uuid "c3cdfeea-ed07-56b9-8520-05327e82865e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517861} {:answer/id #uuid "dd6971fb-f55c-5b45-a29a-c0b1c6b3fce9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "31" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517905} {:answer/id #uuid "f1d38658-fd1d-5ce3-b87a-8e86e685face" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517951}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186517951} :answer-field/id #uuid "202094ff-d5d0-573f-8726-95ed023974e0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517981}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "4429ddaa-a525-58c0-92b3-0e53fe11c811" :question/math-academy-id "q-158687" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,W=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrices $A$ and $W,$ and the vector $b$ above. If the normal equation for the corresponding weighted least-squares problem $W\\,Ax=Wb$ is given by\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}a & 7 \\\\ 7 & b\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ c\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nwhat is the value of $a+b+c?$" :question/worked-solution "To get the normal equation corresponding to $W\\,Ax=Wb,$ we pre-multiply both sides of the equation by $(W\\,A)^{T}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(W\\,A)^{T}\\cdot W\\,Ax & =(W\\,A)^{T}\\cdot Wb \\\\ {A}^{T}({W}^{T}W)Ax & ={A}^{T}({W}^{T}W)b\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since\n\n$$\n{W}^{T}W=[\\begin{aligned}{1}^{2} & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & {3}^{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & {2}^{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 9 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nour normal equation can be written as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 9 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 9 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 9 & 9 \\\\ 4 & -4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -9 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}14 & 7 \\\\ 7 & 17\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -11\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=14+17+(-11)=20.\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "dbe4af0f-6deb-5714-9b84-7310ef2b54a2"}] :activity/title "Weighted Least-Squares" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517493}]}
